<SiteLayout
  title="Now · Puffs of Smoke"
  description="A November 2026 snapshot of what Jon Kohlmeier is working on, writing about, enjoying, and thinking through."
>
  <header class="page-header container-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Now</p>
    <h1>What I’m up to now</h1>
    <p class="page-updated">Updated November 2026.</p>
    <p class="page-header__lede">This is a snapshot of what’s occupying my time and attention lately. It will probably change.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="now-grid container-page">
    <section>
      <p class="section-number">01</p>
      <h2>At work</h2>
      <p>
        I’m the Revenue Operations Lead at West Music, although the work has increasingly stretched beyond the usual
        boundaries of RevOps.
      </p>
      <p>
        Lately I’ve been spending more time on company priorities, customer experience, and helping good ideas survive
        the trip from a meeting to something that actually happens.
      </p>
      <p>
        I’m also thinking quite a bit about AI. Not just what it can automate, but whether it can help people do better
        work without making everything feel more mechanical.
      </p>
      <p>
        One question keeps coming up: How do you help an organization get better without becoming the person responsible
        for fixing everything?
      </p>
      <p>I don’t have a perfect answer yet.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <p class="section-number">02</p>
      <h2>Writing again</h2>
      <p>
        I’ve been rebuilding this website and going through things I wrote years ago. Some of them hold up surprisingly
        well. Others are a good reminder that I’ve changed my mind about a few things.
      </p>
      <p>
        I’d like to write more regularly, without turning writing into another job or worrying too much about whether a
        particular subject fits.
      </p>
      <p>
        Expect thoughts about work and technology alongside things like books, family, faith, and the occasional
        cocktail.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <p class="section-number">03</p>
      <h2>At home</h2>
      <p>
        Life at home revolves around my wife, our young daughter, and the usual assortment of things that come with
        owning a house.
      </p>
      <p>
        I’m trying to be more deliberate about how I spend my evenings and weekends. There always seems to be another
        project, something to repair, or a reason to pick up my phone.
      </p>
      <p>I’d like to get better at leaving some of that unfinished.</p>
      <p>
        I’m also enjoying the small things that make this time of life particularly good. Reading with my daughter, a
        decent cup of coffee, making something worth drinking, and evenings when there’s nowhere else we need to be.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <p class="section-number">04</p>
      <h2>On my mind</h2>
      <p>
        I’m thinking about what meaningful work looks like over the next decade, how to build a stable life without
        making every decision about money, and what it means to be a good husband and father when time and energy are
        limited.
      </p>
      <p>I’m also rediscovering the pleasure of having somewhere to put my thoughts.</p>
      <p>That’s part of why this site exists.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
